---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import news from "../../../data/news/news-2026.js";
import img_Featured from "../../../assets/news/2026/hay-fundraiser.jpg";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import { ClientRouter } from "astro:transitions";

const article = news[0];
const { author, title, content, img, date, id } = article;
---

<ClientRouter />
<Layout title=`${title} - Fallen Oak`>
  <div
    class="bg-[#fefce8] min-h-[calc(100vh-10rem)] px-4 lg:px-0 flex flex-col items-center"
  >
    <a
      class="mt-24 duration-300 hover:bg-blue-200 bg-blue-50 border-2 border-blue-200 hover:border-blue-400 rounded font-semibold text-base px-3 py-1 flex items-center gap-x-2"
      href="../"
      ><Icon name="mdi:arrow-back" class="text-2xl text-blue-600" />Back to News</a
    >
    <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 mx-auto py-8">
      <article class="px-6 mx-auto flex flex-col lg:flex-col gap-x-12 gap-y-8">
        <div class="flex justify-center w-full lg:w-full">
          <Image 
          transition:name={id} src={img_Featured} alt="News" width="400" class="object-cover w-auto h-64 border-2 rounded border-black" />
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-8 w-full lg:w-full">
          <div class="flex flex-col mx-auto gap-y-2 w-full">
            <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold leading-none whitespace-wrap">{title}</h1>
            <p class="text-xs lg:text-sm">
              by
              <span class="text-blue-400">
                <span>{author}</span>
              </span>on
              <time datetime="2021-02-12 15:34:18-0200">{date}</time>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-4 lg:text-base text-sm rounded border border-dashed border-black p-4 bg-amber-100">
            <!-- <p>{content}</p> -->
            <p>As everyone in Florida knows, we are experiencing cold temperatures here, which means lots of hay. The rescue currently has 27 horses between two foster homes: my personal farm, where rehabbing horses are housed, and the 40-acre farm. I provide 850 lb. alfalfa blocks, o/a half blocks, and loose orchard alfalfa hay. Our normal hay bill is approximately $1,500 a week. Right now, it is close to double that.</p>
            <p>This cold snap is due to hang around for the next 12 days, along with it getting even colder this weekend. The rescue was blessed with seven new blankets and neck pieces by a wonderful lady. We are so thankful. Now EVERYONE has a blanket.</p>
            <p>Please donate! Just $20 buys a bale of hay. If you would rather stop in at any J &J tack store and buy a bale or a gift card toward a block please do so, every little bit helps. Let’s get these guys an abundance of hay to keep them warm.</p>
            <p>As always, I am so thankful for ALL my donors, the rescue remains flourishing and taking the horses no one else will with your support. Stay warm all.</p>
            <p><a href="https://donate.fallenoak.org">https://donate.fallenoak.org</a></p>
        </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
